{"kind":"assert","text":"Background for a9551a6d: published in-chat UI guidance is summarized in ~/play/dap-views-prototype/RESEARCH.md, with sources. Four points matter most. (1) Hosts differ on which parts of a tool result reach the view and the model: one host strips structuredContent before the view, others strip _meta. Return only ids and counts, and let the view load details through a view-only tool (visibility app). (2) Write the model's text and tool descriptions as statements of fact about what the view shows, never instructions on how to behave. (3) The published guidance forbids drill-in and Back inside an inline card. The cards prototype deliberately keeps title, details and Back, because it proved the most usable in the trial. Weigh expanding details in place and moving long details to full screen as alternatives, and record the choice in the design. (4) Free text, such as a reason for requesting changes, could pre-fill a chat message rather than a field in the card. Disable superseded copies of a card.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}